[EVIDENCE]
UID: MECH-M4-CLAIMS-REFUTED-AGAINST-THE-TREE
TITLE: The m4 work node claims a registered plugin and a diff-less tool; both are false
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Two claims in the m4 work node (SLICE-CHECKPOINT-WIRING) are false against the
tree, measured 2026-08-28. It says strictdoc's index-build hook is "registered
as ProjectConfig(user_plugin=...) in strictdoc_config.py"; the config passes
project_title, grammars, exclude_doc_paths, formats and dir_for_sdoc_cache
only, and no plugin class exists anywhere (strictdoc_config.py:80-87). It says
the tool "sees the whole graph as it would be after the write, never a diff";
--dry-run prints a unified diff from the disk pre-image and finish() holds
both images per file (sdoc_cli.py:571-582, :650-653) -- what is NOT retained
is the field-level old value (sdoc_model.py:264). Also measured: the plugin
hook, once registered, fires inside every scribe load -- twice per write,
three times per `new` -- and cannot tell a pre-write load from a post-write
verify. The work node's statement is to be corrected when it is rewritten for
the hook layer, not patched here.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Retyped from MECHANISM to EVIDENCE on 2026-08-30 by the mechanism mood test under DEC-NODE-FAMILIES, with high confidence after a second opinion: it records what was observed once, not how something always behaves. Noted for a later split: One universal behaviour sentence a later pass could lift to a MECHANISM: 'the plugin hook, once registered, fires inside every scribe load -- twice per write, three times per new -- and cannot tell a pre-write load from a post-write verify'. 'The work node's statement is to be corrected when it is rewritten' is a work note. The UID keeps its prefix: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE.
